Hiring Team \
Prometheum

Dear Hiring Team,

I am writing to apply for the Software Engineer 1 (Full-Stack) position at Prometheum. My interest in this role is grounded in a project I built during my final year at Portland State University: a full-stack application, written in TypeScript, React, and Python, that converts spoken bar inventory counts into structured data in a relational database. I designed the parsing workflow myself, used AI coding assistants throughout while carefully reviewing and correcting their output, and reduced AI API calls by roughly 80 percent in the process. That same discipline, using AI tools deliberately rather than uncritically, is what I understand this role to require.

The structure of the position is also a strong match for where I am in my career. Starting on small, well-scoped pieces of a TypeScript and React codebase and taking on more responsibility as I build familiarity with the system is precisely the kind of growth path I am looking for.

My coursework in systems programming, data structures, digital circuits, and SQL databases gave me a solid foundation for reasoning about how a request moves from the front end through an API into a database, rather than only recognizing surface-level patterns. I do not have direct experience in finance or blockchain, but I bring a demonstrated ability to learn a new domain quickly and maintain accuracy under scrutiny, skills I developed through prior community research and federal grant reporting work, where documentation had to be correct because other people relied on it directly.

I have also spent several years in fast-paced service roles, most recently as a bar manager, coordinating staff and daily operations under real time pressure. That experience has reinforced strong habits around prioritization, clear communication, and following through on detail-oriented work.

I would welcome the opportunity to bring this combination of full-stack development experience, disciplined use of AI-assisted tools, and a consistent record of learning quickly under pressure to your engineering team. I am happy to discuss the Bar Inventory App or my background in further detail at your convenience.

Sincerely, \
Matt Loera
